    "method": "Not located in imagery. Indian Archaeology 1987-88 (PDF page 25, item 35) gives the ancient site, locally known as Bibino Timbo, as 'Lat 22 deg 54' 40\" N; Long 70 deg 37' 30\" E', 3 km south-east of the present village. That point lies about 0.9 km east of the held 5 km window, which is centred on the village (the site index point). A render of the window's south-east corner shows fields, a canal and a river bend; the fortification could not be recognised."
